cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this course material helped your teaching, please cite it, and cite Stull's book, which it is built on."
title: "practical-meteorology-course: Portuguese undergraduate course material (notes, slides, teacher guide, notebooks) on Stull's Practical Meteorology"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.3"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fabiocampolim-design/practical-meteorology-course"
authors:
  - family-names: Campolim
    given-names: Fabio
keywords:
  - meteorology
  - atmospheric science
  - teaching material
  - Portuguese
  - Jupyter notebooks
  - LaTeX Beamer
  - MetPy
  - climlab
references:
  - type: book
    title: "Practical Meteorology: An Algebra-based Survey of Atmospheric Science"
    authors:
      - family-names: Stull
        given-names: Roland
    year: 2017
    version: "1.02b"
    publisher:
      name: University of British Columbia
    url: "https://www.eoas.ubc.ca/books/Practical_Meteorology/"
    license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  Complete Portuguese teaching material for a two-semester undergraduate course
  on Roland Stull's open textbook Practical Meteorology: for each of the 22
  chapters plus an extra module on climate change, LaTeX lecture notes, Beamer
  slides, a teacher's-guide section, an executed student notebook (four worked
  cases and numerical exercises with MetPy, climlab, SciPy and friends) and a
  solutions notebook (theory checked with SymPy); printable exercise lists, a
  two-semester schedule and a course index. Code is Apache-2.0; the teaching
  content inherits the book's CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
